{
  "id": "027",
  "title": "The Reunion Tour",
  "subtitle": "\"Three years after we signed the divorce papers, my father died. I asked my ex-husband to play at the funeral. He said yes before I finished the sentence.\"",
  "penName": "Denver Lane",
  "genre": "secondChance",
  "hook": "Wes Kellen and I were married for five years. We divorced three years ago, cleanly, at a kitchen table with two lawyers and no blame. He went back to touring. I went back to running my father's guitar shop in Luckenbach, Texas. My father died on a Wednesday in March. I called Wes from the hospital parking lot. He was in Copenhagen. He said *I'll play, Remy, of course* before I got to *would you.* The band flew in Saturday. The grief unfolded. The divorce, it turned out, had been the wrong decision at the right time.",
